==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|tum|ma}}
* {{IPA|/ˈtumːɑ/|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|umːɑ|lang=fi}}

===Adjective===
{{head|fi|adjective|comparative|tummempi|superlative|tummin}}

# [[dark]] [[colour]]
#: ''Hänellä on tumma tukka.''
#:: ''She has dark hair.''
#: ''Naapurin jätkä seurustelee taas sen tumman tytön kanssa.'' 
#:: ''The guy next door is dating the dark-haired girl again.''

====Usage notes====
As an adjective, ''tumma'' normally describes the subject as dark in color: if a person is the subject, it often just means that they have dark hair and possibly dark eyes, not necessarily that their skin color was dark. It also does not necessarily signify that the person in question is Romani.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-koira|tumm|||a|}}

====Antonyms====
* [[vaalea]]

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# (person) [[Gypsy]], [[Rom]]
#: ''Naapurin jätkän tyttökaveri vaikuttaa olevan tumma.''
#:: The girlfriend of the guy next door appears to be a Gypsy.
#: ''Tummat kruisasivat Mersullaan kylän halki.''
#:: The Gypsies cruised through the town in their Mercedes Benz.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-koira|tumm}}

====Usage notes====
As a reference to multiple people, the word is used in the plural case, ''tummat''. When one person is being referred to, the singular case is used.

====Synonyms====
* [[mustalainen]]

